{"title":"1999 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 18","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The equilateral triangle has sides of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/c/2ec701493fa72dda5d6747fe14f30e7b1c2fb6c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2x$\" width=\"19\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/6/856422751144770d42cfd80dde766e9fa2d03a96.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x + 15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"53\" height=\"15\" /> as shown.\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p>The perimeter of the triangle is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/4/664f274a7eb5131e25ba0114db96269465037bec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{ (A) }\\ 15 \\qquad\\text{ (B) }\\ 30 \\qquad\\text{ (C) }\\ 90 \\qquad\\text{ (D) }\\ 45 \\qquad\\text{ (E) }\\ 60$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"433\" height=\"18\" />  \n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>By the definition of an <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Equilateral_triangle\" title=\"Equilateral triangle\">equilateral triangle</a>, all sides of the triangle must be equal to each other. This means that we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/8/bf8de80ff7700be5068b3b9f9b93cd8fdd609393.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2x = x + 15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"96\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p>Subtracting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> from both sides, we get:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/a/89a4662a1dcd96b0a6bc7d5abfe65f22109532a5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 15$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"52\" height=\"13\" />\n</p><p>The perimeter of an equilateral triangle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> times its side length, so the perimeter is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/c/bbc2d5052d87f977fc27bdbbec655976d0613d65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2x \\times 3 = 6x = 6 \\times 15 = \\boxed {\\textbf {(C) } 90}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"259\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017192801\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.011 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.016 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 43/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 440/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 1528/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    5.466      1 Template:Image_needed\n100.00%    5.466      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:32509:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017192801 and revision id 251481. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}